    "body": "the reason i cited those cases is because it's become the norm for custom elements with a `disabled` DOM property to reflect that property to a boolean attribute. This is a well-established cowpath with years or development behind it.\r\n\r\nAccording to this, now, when those libraries move to implement FACE, they will have to keep in mind that `disabled` is a special case and doesn't not follow the usual rules of custom element development. This will be confusing, and the ability to `:host([disabled])` will disappear per spec for FACEs.",
