    "created_at": "2022-10-12T14:48:44Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-10-12T22:47:59Z",
    "body": "> If you're attempting to find out whether the element is disabled, then you should use :disabled instead. Just like on regular form controls, these are two different things.\r\n\r\nI'd be perfectly happy with this if we had a `:state()` selector for custom states. Alas, we don't and it's not uncommon for custom elements to have custom states where valid, invalid, and disabled aren't appropriate. As a stop gap, Shoelace and many other libraries reflect attributes. I understand this is an arguable practice, but short of reflecting attributes or abusing parts for state, we don't have any other options.\r\n\r\nWhat would you recommend as a best practice for custom states? Is there something else in the works for that?",
    "author_association": "NONE",
